Kotimaisten kielten keskus (Institute for the Languages of Finland, "Kotus")

The Kotus files in this directory are data published by Kotus. They are
not covered by the MIT or Apache-2.0 licenses that cover the source of
torille, nor by the GPL that covers the Omorfi/Voikko harness files in
tools/. They are separate works, each published under its own terms, stated
below. The `hyphenation/` subdirectory is not Kotus data; its pattern file
has its own MIT notice, described at the end of this file.


nykysuomensanalista.txt
=======================

Nykysuomen sanalista, the current Finnish word list: over 100,000 word
entries, each a lemma with its homonyms, word class and inflection
information. Tab separated, UTF-8.

This is the Nykysuomen sanalista 2024 published by Kotus. Its official
terms are stated on Kotus's own page for the list:

    Kotimaisten kielten keskus. Nykysuomen sanalista [online].
    Available at
    https://kotus.fi/sanakirjat/kielitoimiston-sanakirja/nykysuomen-sana-aineistot/nykysuomen-sanalista

which states:

    "Sanalista julkaistaan lisenssillä Creative Commons Nimeä 4.0
    Kansainvälinen (CC BY 4.0)."
    (The word list is published under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    International, CC BY 4.0.)

License: CC BY 4.0
    Deed (Finnish): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.fi
    Legal code:     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Source: https://kaino.kotus.fi/lataa/nykysuomensanalista2024.txt

This copy is byte-identical to the 2024 download (md5
27bbd4f3119cb94fcb04a12f11fa799d). No modifications have been made.

Suggested citation (per Kotus's own citation note on the page above):

    Nykysuomen sanalista. Kotimaisten kielten keskus. Saatavissa
    https://kaino.kotus.fi/lataa/nykysuomensanalista2024.txt


kotus-tyypit.txt
================

The Kotus inflectional paradigm table: for each word class, the model word
and the forms each paradigm slot takes, plus the consonant-gradation table.
The file is `include_str!`'d and compiled in; torille reads the paradigm
tables from it at compile time.

What torille actually consumes is only the factual paradigm content. The
code parses the numeric class blocks (classes 1-76, each a set of model
word forms) into `Paradigm`/`Slot` structures; the prose and the gradation
table in the file are skipped by the parser, and the gradation pairs torille
applies at runtime come from a table in `src/kotus.rs`, not from this file.

Copyright does not protect facts. The useful content of this file is a
statement of linguistic facts - that `valo` inflects as `valon, valoa,
valoon`, that class 1 takes the endings it does, and which consonant
alternates with which under gradation. Those facts are true of the Finnish
language and are not original creative expression; stating them, or using
them in code, does not copy any protected expression. It is on that basis,
and only that basis, that the paradigm content is treated as unprotected
facts. The one element that is expression rather than fact is the file's own
introductory prose, and torille does not copy or redistribute that prose; it
is skipped at parse time and the file is reproduced verbatim.

The file carries a Kotus LGPL notice in its header, reproduced here for
completeness; it is not relied on for the use described above.

    Sanalista julkaistaan GNU LGPL -lisenssillä (Lesser General Public
    License). Lisenssiteksti on luettavissa osoitteessa
    http://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl.html.

    Kotimaisten kielten tutkimuskeskus julkaisee taivutustiedoin täydennetyn
    nykysuomen sanalistan. Sanalista ei ole tyhjentävä tai auktoritatiivinen
    luettelo suomen kielen sanoista, vaan sen on tarkoitus mm. toimia
    apuvälineenä suomen kieltä käsittelevien tietokoneohjelmien ja
    suomenkielisten käyttöliittymien kehitystyössä.

If you prefer to rely on a license rather than on the uncopyrightability of
facts, the file's own terms are GNU LGPL; under those terms the file is
redistributed here unmodified with its notice intact, which is compliant.
Either way, torille's own source remains MIT and is not covered by LGPL.

Source: a mirror of the Kotus "sanalistan-kuvaus.txt" file:
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hugovk/everyfinnishword/master/kotus-sanalista_v1/sanalistan-kuvaus.txt

Note on this copy: that mirror is distributed in ISO-8859-1; the copy here
is the same document in UTF-8, which is the encoding its own header says
the list is in. The local file is byte-identical to that mirror once the
mirror is re-encoded from Latin-1 to UTF-8 and CRLF line endings are
normalised. No content was changed.

hyphenation/
=============

`data/hyphenation/hyph-fi-x-school.tex` is the Finnish school
hyphenation pattern set from the `hyph-utf8` project. It is not Kotus
data and is not covered by the terms above.

    title: Hyphenation patterns for Finnish according to the method
           taught in schools
    language: Finnish, school hyphenation (fi-x-school)
    version: 1.0, 2021-03-21
    authors: Teemu Likonen, Arthur Rosendahl
    licence: MIT

The full MIT text is in `data/hyphenation/LICENSE`, and the provenance
is in `data/hyphenation/README.md`. The file is reproduced unmodified.
